    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="post-meta"><time>Last updated: 5 August 2026</time></div>
  </div>
  <div class="post-content">

<p>This page describes how the <strong>Neo Calendar</strong> application (the "app") handles data. The app is a personal, single-user Google Calendar integration that runs on a private home server.</p>

<h2>Data we access</h2>

<p>The app requests <strong>read-only</strong> access to your Google Calendar (<code>calendar.readonly</code> scope). It can view calendar events; it cannot create, modify, or delete them.</p>

<h2>What happens to your data</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Calendar data is read by the app to prepare daily briefings and check for upcoming events.</li>
  <li>Data is processed on private, self-hosted hardware and is <strong>not sold, shared, or disclosed</strong> to any third party.</li>
  <li>Access tokens are stored encrypted on the home server and are used solely to authenticate with Google's APIs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Retention</h2>

<p>No calendar data is stored beyond what is necessary for the app to function. You can revoke access at any time via your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions page</a>.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p>For questions about this policy or the app, contact the app owner by email.</p>

